Fiber executor (fpm-ng): non-blocking ssl/tls stream transports

Everything below is compiled ONLY when HAVE_FPMNG_FIBER_TLS is defined —
fpm-ng's configure sets it for --enable-fpmng-fiber with a static ext/openssl
(sapi/fpmng/config.m4). Without it the files are byte-for-byte upstream.

What changes when it is defined: ssl/sslv3/tls/tlsv1.x factories hand out
streams whose waits (TLS handshake steps, SSL_read/SSL_write retries, the
underlying TCP connect) suspend the fpm-ng request fiber instead of blocking
the process. With pool.executor != fiber, in CLI, and outside a request fiber
the code paths are upstream's, call for call.

How: php_pollfd_for is re-pointed at fpm_pool_fiber_wait_fd for the duration
of the handshake/IO (fpm_fiber_tls_wait). OpenSSL gets SSL_MODE_AUTO_RETRY,
so SSL_read/SSL_write re-drive an in-progress renegotiation themselves and
SSL_want keeps reporting real socket state; upstream cannot use it because a
plain PHP stream must surface the WANT_* condition. The reneg rate limiter
that lived in the WANT_READ path is re-checked explicitly once per handshake
step.

The ssl/tls factories return streams whose ops point DIRECTLY at
php_openssl_socket_ops — no wrapper — so accepted client sockets (allocated
with the listener's ops) and anything comparing against the table see upstream
identity. The fiber wrapper goes on lazily, on the first call from a request
fiber (fpm_fiber_tls_wrap_ops_once), and then stays: the stream belongs to
that request until close.

Refused loudly (E_WARNING + failure, once per process in the log), never
silently blocking:
- "ssl" context option allow_blocking => true on connect;
- server-side ssl/tls transports (STREAM_XPORT_SERVER|BIND) from a request
  fiber: an accepted client inherits the listener's ops and our wrapper's
  close() would free a struct it does not own. The fpm-ng HTTP gateway is
  unaffected — it terminates TLS in libevent, not through these transports.

Waits on: nothing upstream — fpm-ng behavior, gated so upstream is the
default. Expires by redesign (fiber executor dropped, or an upstream async
I/O layer appears).
Checked on: master (cafbcde16205), php-8.5.9.

